[goer@quads.uchicago.edu (Richard L. Goerwitz) writes:]
[] Incidentally, regarding my earlier question about fountains:  We
[] have found out that, after drinking at one, mysterious things begin
[] to happen.  If it dries up, for instance, a thing in your inventory
[] might become cursed that wasn't before.  Similar, though opposite,
[] things can happen if the fountain happens to have been a good one.
[] It is indeed tricky figuring out whether to drink from one or not.
[] So far we haven't found a consistent way of being sure whether to
[] do it or not.  Another problem is avoiding water nymphs, which are
[] sometimes attracted when you quaff from the fountain.

it's strange how the mind plays tricks on you.  there's no a priori
good or bad fountain.  the effects are randomly determined during
the interaction.  the messages may or may not be relevant, you have
to be observant to decipher this. one message, somehting to the effect
that this water is no good means that something in your inventory
has just become cursed.  that's what you noticed after the fountain
disappeared.  monsters may appear from fountains and this can be deadly
(as with most things in the dungeon), so you'd best prepare.  engraving
`Elbereth' at the site of the fountain might help (as long as the
engraving stays intact).  and then again a grateful demon might appear
and give you a wish.  what do think might happen if you dipped a long
sword into a fountain (your name need not be Arthur)?  strange huh ...

[] The questions we had over dinner amounted to:
[]
[]  1) Whaddya do with sinks, other than drink and wash?

while "washing" your ring could slip from your finger and drop down
the drain.  in the dungeon, when this happens (drop ring down drain)
the sink reacts in different ways and the experienced hacker can
determine from these reactions the type of ring lost.  btw, i asked
a gnomish wizard about this and he says that a sink can sink you
when you're in an elevated mood (i think he said mood).  what do
wizards know anyway ...

isn't quaffing alone problem enough (especially considering the toxic
waste problems)???

[]  2) What does it mean if you hear bubbling water, or water
[]      falling on coins?

you'll notice a pattern of messages corresponding to events (but not
always!).  i think these messages refer to the (initial) presence of a
fountain on your level.  obviously, if you hear someone cursing
shoplifters and later you hear the chime of a register then there's
a shop somewhere on the level, and so on ...

[]  3) Is there any advantage to being Lawful, Neutral, or
[]      Chaotic, other than that it affects your interaction
[]      with similarly aligned monsters and altars?

the different alignments allow different (subtle) behaviors.  this
is a whole 'nother subject which i'm going to skip for now.  it would
be most beneficial to a "novice" to be lawful (which doesn't require
that you start the game that way, a whole 'nother subject ...) since
lawful altars can be used to _create_ holy water.  this is only true
of water and altars. don't think about it, just do it (bo knows altars
and all that).

[]  4) Why should we ever wash anything?

is there a command for wash? i'm aware of #dip and #wipe which
is used when you have cream pie filling smeared on your face.  umm,
Keystone Kops throw cream pies.  umm, umm, the Kops protect the
shops from thieves.  you weren't planning on stealing anything from
a shop were you?  nooo, i didn't think so ...

[] One comment my son had was that it seemed silly that so much effort
[] got spent on finding food to relieve hunger, and yet thirst went un-
[] noticed.  I agree.  I've also noticed that the juices, which you'd
[] think would alleviate hunger in many cases (e.g. slime mold juice),
[] don't seem to affect your hunger status.  Dis don' make no sense.

and so the debate continues ...

actually the food issue gets easier as you go deeper but ironically
you shouldn't do this too fast at first.  you can also eat freshly
killed corpses that aren't poisonous (unless you feel healthy and
are poison resistant,  see your doctor about this).  in a pinch,
if all is well, a prayer can fill your stomach (but as with all
things in the dungeon this can backfire also).

